  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When a storm hits and damages your home's interior, it can be really overwhelming, right? Your first priority is always safety. Don't rush into areas that might have electrical hazards, gas leaks, or structural weaknesses like sagging ceilings. Once you've confirmed it's safe, the next crucial step is to document everything. Grab your phone and take lots of photos and videos of the damage before you touch anything. This documentation is super important for your insurance claim later on. You should also get in touch with your insurer as soon as possible, ideally within a few hours. They can guide you on the next steps for temporary mitigation, like tarping a damaged roof or boarding up windows. Remember, only approve temporary fixes initially. Starting permanent repairs too soon can complicate your insurance claim. For anything serious, especially if there's significant structural damage or active water coming in, calling in professionals like HH Remodeling LLC can make a huge difference. We can help you navigate this tough situation and get your home on the road to recovery."
    }
  ],
